{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789207275,"nonce":"W0CFS6JMDeHHtUH5bt1TnVdLGAo=","message":"Measured again at 28168f4, which adds the counters permanently (ASH_PROFILE=phases: 'air instrs translated', 'air instrs rebuilt as opcodes', 'opcodes translated'). AOT builds:\n\n    test_basic       7205 AIR instrs, 2858 rebuilt as opcodes  (40%)\n    test_stdlib     10225 AIR instrs, 4551 rebuilt              (45%)\n    bench_deltablue  8726 AIR instrs, 3674 rebuilt              (42%)\n\nWhat translate_air_v2 lowers directly: Param, Const*, Mov/Copy of values, the arithmetic and compare ops, shifts, GetGlobal/SetGlobal, Fma, the five vector ops, Pos, and every terminator and phi edge. Everything else still goes through air_instr_opcode -\u003e translate_opcode. On test_stdlib, by instruction:\n\n    Call 1025  FieldGet 1002  FieldSet 789  Cast 358  New 236  NullCheck 226\n    CellSet 215  CellGet 154  MemGet 127  MemSet 111  CallMethod 61  CellRef 40\n    CallClosure 34  ArraySize 33  CellIncr 28  GetTID 22  GetType 21  MakeEnum 20\n    InstanceClosure 12  EnumField 8  Intrinsic 7  EnumIndex 5  Unref 4  DynSet 4\n    StaticClosure 3  CellDecr 2  EnumAlloc 1  EndTrap 1  DynGet 1\n\nSo the remaining work is the object model and calls: field access, the call family, casts, allocation, null checks, cells and memory ops. FieldGet/FieldSet and SetEnumField still carry the two workarounds this issue names (regs[ri] overwrite, fabricated EnumAlloc). The Cranelift side (codegen.rs) translates every AIR instruction directly; only the LLVM tier round-trips.","files":null}]}